assistant: Subject: Convert cents to dollars for vendor API 2026-10-01

The vendor API version 2026-10-01 returns product prices in cents (119900) where version 2026-01-01 returned dollars (1199), and `search_products` passed `price` through unchanged. The spec in `vendor/openapi.json` didn't change and the repo has no changelog, so the cents reading comes from the recorded data alone: every new price is exactly 100× the matching v1 fixture (1199→119900, 749.5→74950). The fix in `src/tools/search_products.ts` reads the `vendor-api-version` response header and divides `price` by 100 when it is 2026-10-01 or later. Responses without that header, including the v1 fixtures, give exactly the same output as before. Typecheck, lint and all 13 tests pass, but no test covers the new version. Two loose ends: no recorded call shows whether `get_product` and `get_order` got the same change, and they are unchanged. Also, a newer vendor version that switches back to dollars would get divided by 100 by mistake.

